<title>UK: Harvey Nichols up, analyst ups target price.</title>
<headline>Harvey Nichols up, analyst ups target price.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Harvey Nichols rose on Monday as analysts at Morgan Stanley raised their price target for the shares based on upwards revisions to sales estimates for the group.</p>
<p>The shares were up 10p at 372-1/2p by 1220 GMT but trading volume remained thin.</p>
<p>&quot;We have raised our 1996/7 forecasts for the group due to better than expected sales growth and good cost control,&quot; said Victoria Melendez, stores analyst at Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p>&quot;Our new target price for the shares is 400p, up from 376p before,&quot; she added.</p>
</text>
